---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SearchBox from '../../components/SearchBox.astro';
import potions from '../../data/potions.json';
---
<Base title="Minecraft Potions: Every Brewing Recipe" description="Every Minecraft potion recipe: ingredients, effects, durations and the best uses. Brewing basics, splash and lingering variants, Java and Bedrock." canonicalPath="/potions/">
  <div class="container">
    <nav class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Potions</nav>
    <h1>Minecraft Potions</h1>
    <p class="sub">{potions.length} potions with exact brewing recipes, durations and when to use them.</p>
    <SearchBox placeholder="Search potions, items, guides..." />
    <div class="quick-answer"><strong>Quick answer:</strong> place a brewing stand, fuel it with blaze powder, and brew nether wart into water bottles to make Awkward Potions - the base of almost every potion. Add the effect ingredient (see each potion below), then modify: redstone extends duration, glowstone amplifies to level II, gunpowder makes it splash, and dragon's breath makes splash lingering.</div>
    <h2>Brewing basics</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Brewing stand:</strong> 1 blaze rod + 3 cobblestone-tier blocks. Each blaze powder fuels 20 brewing operations.</li>
      <li><strong>Awkward Potion</strong> (nether wart + water bottle) is the base of everything except Weakness, which brews a fermented spider eye straight into a water bottle.</li>
      <li><strong>Modifiers:</strong> redstone = longer, glowstone = stronger (pick one), gunpowder = throwable splash, dragon's breath = lingering cloud (for tipped arrows).</li>
      <li><strong>Fermented spider eye</strong> corrupts effects: Swiftness becomes Slowness, Healing becomes Harming, Night Vision becomes Invisibility.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="grid-cards" style="margin-top:24px">
      {potions.map(p => (
        <a class="card" href={`/potions/${p.slug}/`}>
          <h3>{p.name.replace('Potion of ','')}</h3>
          <p>{p.effect.split(' - ')[1] || p.effect}</p>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
